---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About TRACED | Jonathan R. Reed Data Breach Archive Project"
  description="Learn how Jonathan R. Reed built TRACED as a static public breach archive using Have I Been Pwned data, client-side password checking, and privacy-first design."
>
  <Nav currentPath="/about/" />

  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1" class="page">
    <div class="wrap about">
      <header class="page-head">
        <h1>About TRACED</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          TRACED is a weekend project. I wanted a better way to browse the
          <a href="https://haveibeenpwned.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Have I Been Pwned<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
          dataset, and the case-file format felt like a good fit.
        </p>
        <p class="byline">
          <img
            src="https://img.jonathanrreed.com/personal/jonathan.avif"
            alt=""
            width="48"
            height="48"
            class="byline-photo"
            onerror="this.style.display='none'"
          />
          <span>
            By <a href="https://jonathanrreed.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Jonathan R. Reed<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
          </span>
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose">
        <section>
          <h2>What this is</h2>
          <p>
            A browser for the Have I Been Pwned breach database, set up like a case-file archive. Each breach gets its
            own page with dates, the number of affected accounts, the data that was exposed, and how long HIBP took to
            list it.
          </p>
          <p>
            It doesn't replace HIBP. It's another way to read public breach history, and a reminder that old accounts
            tend to outlive the services they were made for.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>How it works</h2>
          <dl class="how">
            <div>
              <dt>Pre-built pages</dt>
              <dd>
                Every breach page is generated at build time from HIBP's public breach feed. No app server or database
                sits behind it.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>No tracking</dt>
              <dd>
                No analytics, no cookies and no behavioral tracking. TRACED adds no logging or profiling of its own.
                Hosting providers may keep standard request logs.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Password check</dt>
              <dd>
                Your browser hashes the password and sends only the first 5 characters of the hash. The password itself
                never leaves your device.
              </dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Data sources</h2>
          <p>
            Everything here comes from Troy Hunt's Have I Been Pwned, a public breach database he has run since 2013.
          </p>

          <div class="sources">
            <article class="source">
              <h3>Have I Been Pwned</h3>
              <p>
                The main breach database. Every publicly known breach, with dates, the number of affected accounts,
                the data taken and whether the breach is verified. Free, no API key.
              </p>
              <ul class="endpoints data">
                <li>GET haveibeenpwned.com/api/v3/breaches</li>
                <li>GET haveibeenpwned.com/api/v3/breach/{'{name}'}</li>
              </ul>
              <a href="https://haveibeenpwned.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">haveibeenpwned.com<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
            </article>

            <article class="source">
              <h3>Pwned Passwords</h3>
              <p>
                Hundreds of millions of real passwords exposed in past breaches. The password checker uses this API
                with k-anonymity, so the full password or hash is never sent.
              </p>
              <ul class="endpoints data">
                <li>GET api.pwnedpasswords.com/range/{'{prefix}'}</li>
              </ul>
              <a href="https://haveibeenpwned.com/Passwords" target="_blank" rel="noopener">haveibeenpwned.com/Passwords<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
            </article>
          </div>

          <p class="muted">
            All the data belongs to Troy Hunt and Have I Been Pwned. TRACED is an independent front end, not affiliated
            with or endorsed by HIBP.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Built with</h2>
          <p>
            Astro 5 for the static pages, React 19 for the interactive parts, Tailwind CSS v4 and
            <a href="https://starwind.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Starwind UI<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
            for styling and components, and Cloudflare Pages for hosting.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .byline {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
  }

  .byline-photo {
    width: 3rem;
    height: 3rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    object-fit: cover;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .how {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .how dt {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    letter-spacing: var(--display-tracking);
  }

  .how dd {
    margin: 0.15rem 0 0;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
  }

  .sources {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .source {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--card);
  }

  .source h3 {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
  }

  .source p {
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
  }

  .endpoints {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    word-break: break-all;
  }

  .endpoints li {
    padding: 0.35rem 0.6rem;
    background: var(--muted);
    border-radius: 0.375rem;
  }
</style>
